  "full_response": "1. Identify all PROPRIETARY information before handling it, including data, documents and communication.\n2. Segregate PROPRIETARY information from non-proprietary information within the organization.\n3. Ensure only authorized personnel have access to PROPRIETARY information.\n4. Implement secure storage methods for PROPRIETARY information, such as encrypted drives or secure servers.\n5. Restrict transmission of PROPRIETARY information to secure methods, such as encrypted email or secure messaging systems.\n6. Train employees on handling and recognizing PROPRIETARY information to comply with company policies and legal obligations.\n7. Maintain detailed records of who has access to and the usage PROPRIETARY information.\n8. Use strong, updated authentication methods (passwords, two-step verification, etc.) to protect access to PROPRIARY information.\n9. Securely dispose of any PROPRIETARY information that is no longer needed (shredding, incineration).\n10. Regularly review and update security protocols related to managing PROPRIETARY information to ensure ongoing compliance.",
